    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493309472/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Thursday, April 19, 1906
Cold. Fine.
Music in morning. Lots of people came in afternoon hear Tovey play. Miss Weisse stayed to dine, but Bernhard and I went in to a very dull dinner at the Serristoris.
Friday, April 20, 1906
Cold. Fine.
Music in morning.
Placci and Miss Weisse to lunch. Discussion.
Gurds  called! Rembelinski came for talk with B.B. We all went down to Placci’s and heard Buonamici play. I like both Tovey and Kelly. Tovey is a marvel, a most intellectual person, but very impersonal. Kelly is very young, but quite the kind of person I like.
Saturday, April 21, 1906
Cold. Fine. Cool.
B.B. took Lady Sassoon to Pitti and lunched with her, and called on Mrs. Cooper Hewitt and the Serristori. Miss Weisse came up and we went to the Gamberaia. She’s awfully tactless and fussy and Kelly is wild with her.
Sunday, April 22, 1906
Rain. Day of music.
Mrs. Hewitt lunch, ____  after
Hapgoods to dine. Tovey talked splendidly.
Wrote Arcangeli, Lady Henry, Mother, F.B."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 71 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1906> .

